**Program.cs** — stdio transport with DI:

```csharp
using Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection;
using Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting;
using Microsoft.Extensions.Logging;

var builder = Host.CreateApplicationBuilder(args);

// CRITICAL: log to stderr only — stdout is the JSON-RPC transport
builder.Logging.AddConsole(options =>
    options.LogToStandardErrorThreshold = LogLevel.Trace);

builder.Services.AddHttpClient("MyApi", client =>
{
    client.BaseAddress = new Uri("https://api.example.com");
});

builder.Services.AddMcpServer()
    .WithStdioServerTransport()
    .WithToolsFromAssembly();

await builder.Build().RunAsync();
```

**ApiTools.cs** — tool class wrapping a REST API:

```csharp
using System.ComponentModel;
using System.Text.Json;
using Microsoft.Extensions.Logging;
using ModelContextProtocol.Server;

[McpServerToolType]
public class ApiTools(IHttpClientFactory httpFactory, ILogger<ApiTools> logger)
{
    [McpServerTool, Description("Fetch a resource by its unique identifier.")]
    public async Task<string> GetResource(
        [Description("The unique resource ID")] string id,
        CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)
    {
        logger.LogInformation("Fetching resource {Id}", id);
        var client = httpFactory.CreateClient("MyApi");
        return await client.GetStringAsync($"/resources/{id}", cancellationToken);
    }

    [McpServerTool, Description("Search resources by keyword query.")]
    public async Task<string> SearchResources(
        [Description("Search keyword")] string query,
        [Description("Max results to return (1-50)")] int limit = 10,
        CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)
    {
        var client = httpFactory.CreateClient("MyApi");
        var response = await client.GetStringAsync(
            $"/resources?q={Uri.EscapeDataString(query)}&limit={limit}",
            cancellationToken);
        return response;
    }

    [McpServerTool(ReadOnly = true), Description("List all available resource categories.")]
    public async Task<string> ListCategories(
        CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)
    {
        var client = httpFactory.CreateClient("MyApi");
        return await client.GetStringAsync("/categories", cancellationToken);
    }
}
```

---

### How DI works for MCP tools

The SDK supports **two injection styles**:

| Style | How it works |
|-------|-------------|
| **Constructor injection** (non-static class, shown above) | The class receives DI services via its primary constructor. The SDK instantiates the class per-call using the DI container. |
| **Method parameter injection** (static class) | DI services appear as method parameters alongside tool parameters. |

**Key rule:** The SDK automatically distinguishes tool parameters from injected services. Types registered in DI (`HttpClient`, `ILogger<T>`, `IMcpServer`, `CancellationToken`, `IProgress<>`) are resolved from the container and **never appear** in the tool's JSON schema shown to the LLM. Only parameters with `[Description]` are exposed to the LLM.

So in `GetResource` above, the LLM sees only `id` — `CancellationToken` is injected, and `IHttpClientFactory`/`ILogger` come from the constructor.
